# Hamro3D — Nuxt 3 Engineering Standards

## Framework Stack

- **Nuxt 3** (latest stable) — SSR/ISR hybrid rendering
- **Vue 3** — Composition API with `<script setup lang="ts">` exclusively
- **TypeScript** — strict mode, no `any` types
- **Tailwind CSS v4** — `@theme` tokens mapped to Hamro3D design system
- **Pinia** — global state management
- **Nitro** — server routes and API layer

## Vue Component Rules

### Always
- Use `<script setup lang="ts">` — no Options API, no `defineComponent()`
- Define props with `defineProps<T>()` — TypeScript interface, not runtime validators
- Define emits with `defineEmits<T>()`
- Use `computed()` for derived state, not methods
- Use `watchEffect()` or `watch()` sparingly — prefer computed
- Template refs: `const el = useTemplateRef<HTMLElement>('el')`

### Never
- No `this` keyword — Composition API only
- No `<style>` blocks — Tailwind utilities only (rare exceptions must be scoped)
- No `v-html` unless content is sanitized server-side
- No barrel exports (`index.ts`) in component directories — Nuxt auto-imports

### Component File Order
```
<script setup lang="ts"> ... </script>
<template> ... </template>
```

## Naming Conventions

| Entity | Convention | Example |
|--------|-----------|---------|
| Components | PascalCase, `H3d` prefix | `H3dButton.vue`, `H3dProductCard.vue` |
| Pages | kebab-case | `our-story.vue`, `[slug].vue` |
| Composables | camelCase, `use` prefix | `useCommission.ts`, `useCollection.ts` |
| Server routes | kebab-case with method suffix | `index.get.ts`, `[id].get.ts`, `submit.post.ts` |
| Pinia stores | camelCase, `use` prefix, `Store` suffix | `useCartStore.ts`, `useAuthStore.ts` |
| Types/Interfaces | PascalCase | `Piece`, `Commission`, `Collection` |
| Utilities | camelCase | `formatPrice.ts`, `slugify.ts` |

## Directory Structure

```
app/
├── components/
│   ├── ui/           # H3dButton, H3dInput, H3dBadge, H3dModal
│   ├── layout/       # H3dNavbar, H3dFooter, H3dHero, H3dSection
│   ├── product/      # H3dProductCard, H3dProductGallery, H3dPriceTag
│   ├── commission/   # H3dCommissionForm, H3dCommissionSteps
│   └── shared/       # H3dLogo, H3dLanguageSwitcher, H3dLoadingReveal
├── composables/      # Auto-imported composables
├── layouts/          # default.vue, checkout.vue
├── pages/            # File-based routing
├── plugins/          # Client/server plugins
├── middleware/        # Route middleware
├── stores/           # Pinia stores
├── types/            # Shared TypeScript interfaces
└── utils/            # Auto-imported utility functions
server/
├── api/              # Nitro API routes
├── middleware/        # Server middleware
├── utils/            # Server-only utilities
└── plugins/          # Server lifecycle plugins
```

## Data Fetching

```typescript
// Page-level data — SSR-rendered
const { data } = await useFetch('/api/pieces')

// With transform and error handling
const { data: piece, error } = await useFetch(`/api/pieces/${route.params.id}`, {
  transform: (raw) => parsePiece(raw),
})

// Client-side actions (event handlers only)
async function submitCommission(payload: CommissionPayload) {
  await $fetch('/api/commission', { method: 'POST', body: payload })
}
```

- Always `await` the `useFetch` / `useAsyncData` call at the top level of `<script setup>`
- Use `transform` to shape API responses
- Handle errors with `error` ref and show branded error states

## Server Routes (Nitro)

```typescript
// server/api/pieces/index.get.ts
export default defineEventHandler(async (event) => {
  const pieces = await fetchPieces()
  return pieces
})

// server/api/commission/index.post.ts
import { z } from 'zod'

const CommissionSchema = z.object({
  pieceId: z.string().uuid(),
  name: z.string().min(1),
  message: z.string().optional(),
})

export default defineEventHandler(async (event) => {
  const body = await readValidatedBody(event, CommissionSchema.parse)
  const commission = await createCommission(body)
  return commission
})
```

- Validate all inputs with Zod via `readValidatedBody` / `getValidatedQuery`
- Return proper HTTP status: `createError({ statusCode: 404, message: '...' })`
- Keep business logic in `server/utils/` — handlers should be thin

## Rendering Strategy

Configure in `nuxt.config.ts` via `routeRules`:

```typescript
routeRules: {
  '/':                  { isr: 3600 },      // Homepage — ISR 1hr
  '/collections/**':    { isr: 3600 },      // Collections — ISR 1hr
  '/piece/**':          { isr: 600 },       // Pieces — ISR 10min
  '/commission':        { ssr: true },       // Commission — always fresh SSR
  '/api/**':            { cors: true },      // API — CORS enabled
}
```

## SEO Pattern

Every page must include:

```typescript
useSeoMeta({
  title: 'Page Title — Hamro3D',
  description: 'Warm, brand-voice description',
  ogTitle: 'Page Title — Hamro3D',
  ogDescription: 'Warm, brand-voice description',
  ogImage: '/og/page-name.jpg',
  ogType: 'website',
  ogLocale: 'en_NP',
  twitterCard: 'summary_large_image',
})
```

## i18n

- Default locale: `en`
- Supported: `['en', 'ne']`
- All user-facing strings use `$t('key')` in templates or `t('key')` in script
- Devanagari containers get `lang="ne"` attribute
- Locale files in `i18n/locales/en.json` and `i18n/locales/ne.json`

## Error Handling

- Use `<NuxtErrorBoundary>` in layouts with branded fallback
- Create `error.vue` at app root with brand-styled error page
- Server errors return warm copy, never raw status codes
- Log errors server-side, show human messages client-side

## Testing Guidance

- Component tests with Vitest + Vue Test Utils
- Server route tests with Vitest + `$fetch` against test server
- E2E with Playwright for critical flows (commission, navigation)
